## Journey: Validate from Tasks

Clerk opens a case, uses **Next steps** on an assigned task, completes **Validate application form**, then returns to Case details.

Yellow outline marks the Next steps control that starts the journey. Hover blocks for element names.

<div class="bf-journey">
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_tasks", locals: { caption: "1. TEC PCN — Tasks", highlight: true } %></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Next steps</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_validate_form", locals: { caption: "2. Event — Validate application form" } %></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Submit</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_case_details", locals: { caption: "3. TEC PCN — Case details" } %></div>
</div>

## Journey: Edit application from Next steps

Same Tasks entry point; Next steps opens a form-specific edit event (TE9 / PE3 / TE7 / PE2 share one blockframe shape). After submit, Case details shows the updated sections.

